cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you refer to this network, please cite it as below.
title: Digraphs of real orthogonal upper Hessenberg matrices
abstract: >-
  Which directed graphs arise as the zero / non-zero pattern of an unreduced
  real orthogonal upper Hessenberg matrix. Every such matrix is a product of
  adjacent Givens rotations up to signs, its support digraph is determined by
  the active set S of angles with non-vanishing cosine, and S is recoverable
  from the digraph whenever it has at least two elements — so the isomorphism
  classes number 2^(n-1) - floor((n-1)/2), and the loopless ones
  F_(n-1) - floor((n-3)/2). A pre-formalization network: the argument in
  prose, with every statement it turns on as a separate addressable card and
  the dependencies between those statements as edges, beside the Lean 4
  library that formalizes it.
